<Resolution />

## What to do now

Keep the shared parser and booking-v3 hint as separate historical issues. Engineering reports the parser fixed and the booking-v3 form retired, so close the first as completed and the second as not planned. The retired hint was not repaired. These dispositions follow the new desk update rather than a local production change. The scenario mentions about 300,000 calendar users; that is product reach, not the number of affected users measured by this export.

The [subject-only triage rule](/kb/triage/dedupe/) and [accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) are historical evidence. Their old review dates exceed the KB freshness threshold. Keep the accepted decision immutable. [Proposed decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/) would supersede it: compare tenant, locale, form and channel, and read contradictory report bodies before merging. A matching subject is neither necessary nor sufficient evidence of a shared cause. The proposal has not yet been accepted by the desk.

## Check the deduplication rule

<DedupeExplorer />

The explorer evaluates the exported cause logic. Unknown tenants remain unplaced, so they must be investigated instead of automatically merged. Different subjects can have the same cause, and identical subjects can describe different causes.

## Evidence and next review

The raw sources remain in `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`, `src/lib/data/tenants/` and `src/lib/data/desk-notes.json`. Exported classification is in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`. The independent analysis used by this page is in `src/lib/solution/analysis.ts`. The preparation manifest records source SHA256 values in `evidence/source-sha256.json`, and the issue drafts and full membership lists are in `issues/` and `evidence/`. Counts on this page are recomputed from the loaded report and tenant files on every build; update the sources and rebuild instead of editing numbers in prose.

Next, obtain a fresh export, compare memberships by report id and re-review the timing notes against booking timestamps, invite payloads and timezone information. A changed count or a newly demonstrated cause requires updated issues and a rebuilt page. The public issues link to the distinct dispositions above. The first course claim accepted both tickets but did not solve the challenge. This page records the new engineering report and does not claim that gpt-6.1-sol changed production.

